          "raw_display": "Okay so here's what we're doing, I need you to help me walk through the lockout before we sign anything. First, the main breaker for Station Three is right there on the disconnect panel, the big red handle on the left side, you pull that all the way down to the off position, you'll feel a little click when it seats. Then, and this is the part that matters, you take your personal lock, the red one with your name on it, and you put it on that breaker so nobody can flip it back up while I'm in there. Now I'm gonna attach my hazard tag right next to yours, it's got my name and the date on it, so make sure you can see both of them. After that you walk over to the local control panel, the one down at the station, and you hit the start button, it should do nothing, no spin up, no lights, that's your zero energy check. If anything moves or you hear a hum, stop, tell me right away, we don't go further. Last thing, the conveyor, you need to confirm it's in manual mode, not auto, so the two hundred and forty brackets sitting on the inbound side don't start feeding into a dead station. You see the mode switch up there, flip it to manual, and that's it, we're clear to work the area. You follow so far, or do you want me to go over any of that again before we lock it down?",
